# Enforce LF line endings for all text files on checkout across all
# platforms (including Windows). Without this, git converts LF to CRLF
# for text-classified files on Windows checkout, which breaks:
#   - server/init.test.ts template drift guard (byte-comparison)
#   - the npm-pack shape assertion (byte-comparison of tarball entries)
# See openspec/changes/add-windows-ci-matrix/design.md D4.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary patterns — never treat as text, never touch line endings.
*.png    -text
*.jpg    -text
*.jpeg   -text
*.gif    -text
*.ico    -text
*.icns   -text
*.pdf    -text
*.woff   -text
*.woff2  -text
*.ttf    -text
*.otf    -text
*.dmg    -text
*.exe    -text
*.vsix   -text
*.tgz    -text
*.zip    -text
*.node   -text
